WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.000
Speaker 1: There are only so many major political
events globally each year, and we have one

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.920
that is transpiring right now.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:11.049
The British Prime Minister, Boris Johnson
of the Conservative Party, colloquially known

00:00:11.049 --> 00:00:14.160
as the Tories, has announced that he's going
to resign.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.750
His party has lost confidence in him.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.300
It has been humiliation after humiliation.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.970
And up until the last moment, Boris Johnson
was saying resign, why?

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:23.600
No, why would I resign?

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.690
And he has now resigned or he will resign
once a replacement is found.

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:33.250
A very good report about this from the Associated
Press.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:37.750
Britain's Boris Johnson resigning as prime
minister amid scandal.

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:41.170
This is another Trumpist type.

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:46.400
Whose political run is, at least for now,
ending in completely humiliating defeat.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:50.270
Of course, you know, pending what happens
with Trump in 2024, there may be more written

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:57.100
in the Trump story, but this is another Trump
in type who is getting humiliated out of office.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:58.100
Prime Minister Boris.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:03.880
Boris Johnson announced his resignation Thursday
amid a mass revolt by top members of his government,

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:09.420
marking an end to three tumultuous years in
power in which he brazenly bent and sometimes

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.000
broke the rules of British politics.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.220
Months of defiance ended, almost with a shrug
as Johnson stood in ten Downing Street and

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.770
conceded that his party wanted him gone.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:21.580
Let's look at a bit of that announcement.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:28.850
And yeah, I the AP very accurately saying
it was months of defiance and this sort of

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:32.730
faux principled, indignant defiance of resign.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:35.689
I am here to do a job for the people of the.

00:01:35.689 --> 00:01:36.799
Yeah, I guess I'm gone.

00:01:36.799 --> 00:01:37.799
No, no, no.

00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:38.799
Unidentified: Good afternoon.

00:01:38.799 --> 00:01:39.799
Thank you.

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:40.799
Thank you.

00:01:40.799 --> 00:01:41.799
It is clearly now the will.

00:01:41.799 --> 00:01:50.710
Speaker 2: Of the Parliamentary Conservative
Party that there should be a new leader of

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:53.400
that party and therefore a new prime minister.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:58.970
I have agreed with Sir Graham Brady, the chairman
of our backbench MPs, that the process of

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:05.450
choosing that new leader should begin now
and the timetable will be announced next week.

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:10.700
And today appointed a cabinet to serve, as
I will, until a new leader is in place.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:17.260
So I want to say to the millions of people
who voted for us in 2019, many of them voting

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:19.720
conservative for the first time.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:21.880
Thank you for that incredible mandate.

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:22.880
Speaker 1: Yeah.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:27.150
I mean, the message should be to those who
voted for the Tories for the first time.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:29.290
You're probably never going to do it again.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:33.720
Speaker 2: The biggest conservative majority
since 1987.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.709
The biggest share of the vote since 1979.

00:02:36.709 --> 00:02:39.680
Speaker 1: Yeah.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.230
So there it is.

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:43.400
Boris Johnson resigning in shame.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:46.510
A little bit more from the Associated Press
article.

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:50.489
The brash 58 year old who took Britain out
of the EU and steered it through COVID and

00:02:50.489 --> 00:02:55.520
the war in Ukraine was brought down by one
scandal too many, this one involving his appointment

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:58.620
of a politician who had been accused of sexual
misconduct.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:03.819
Now, I have to tell you, in reading through
this, Johnson is a sort of British version

00:03:03.819 --> 00:03:11.810
of Trump in many ways, not just the hair,
the kind of brash, never apologize type nature

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:14.300
and, you know, the sort of pseudo right wing
stuff.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.300
Yeah.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:20.030
But I have to tell you, at this point, American
politics has fallen so far, like into the

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:21.769
toilet, for lack of a better term.

00:03:21.769 --> 00:03:24.950
Speaker 2: People are flushing toilets ten
times, 15 times.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:29.450
Speaker 1: American politics are so in the
toilet that if Trump had done the exact same

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:33.650
things Johnson did, I don't know that it would
have been even a fraction of the big deal

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:36.420
that it became in the UK.

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:40.140
The messiest of prime ministers did not leave
cleanly, the article says.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:44.470
Johnson stepped down immediately as Conservative
Party leader, but said he would remain as

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:47.519
prime minister until the party chooses his
successor.

00:03:47.519 --> 00:03:49.930
The timetable could be announced next week.

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:53.909
From what I'm reading, we could be talking
about months during which it's a sort of lame

00:03:53.909 --> 00:03:57.930
duck by by self designations situation there.

00:03:57.930 --> 00:03:59.680
He could be there for months.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:02.160
Still, many in the party wanted him gone before
then.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:06.739
His government has been shredded by scores
of resignations, and there's a long, long

00:04:06.739 --> 00:04:07.739
list of those.

00:04:07.739 --> 00:04:12.160
Johnson clung to power for two days, defiantly
telling lawmakers Wednesday he had a colossal

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:15.180
mandate from voters massive dumps of votes.

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:18.849
He had guys and intended to get on with the
business of government.

00:04:18.849 --> 00:04:23.680
But he was forced to concede defeat Thursday
after one of his closest allies, newly appointed

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:29.330
Treasury chief Nadhim Zahawi, publicly told
him to resign for the good of the country.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.690
Look at these numbers.

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:35.919
About 50 cabinet secretaries, ministers and
lower level officials had quit the government

00:04:35.919 --> 00:04:42.569
over the past few days, often castigating
the prime minister for his lack of integrity.

00:04:42.569 --> 00:04:51.059
So a very interesting and big story, the real
the most relevant question arguably globally

00:04:51.059 --> 00:04:59.080
about this resignation is, okay, so you've
replaced Johnson with someone less cartoonish,

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:06.520
but does the UK's positioning in geopolitics
change on any major issue?

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:10.499
Does the trade relationships change in any
major way as a result of this?

00:05:10.499 --> 00:05:12.599
No, probably not.

00:05:12.599 --> 00:05:18.719
Does the British position on the Ukrainian
defense against the Russian invasion change?

00:05:18.719 --> 00:05:20.999
No, probably not.

00:05:20.999 --> 00:05:29.129
And so it is a very it's a personally scandal
ridden individual who's now going to be replaced.

00:05:29.129 --> 00:05:36.280
But there's really no reason to think that
in any substantive capacity, the UK's geopolitical

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:38.369
positioning is going to change.

00:05:38.369 --> 00:05:42.560
And you could say, well, that's a good thing
or that's a bad thing, or stability is good,

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:46.499
but actually change would be good because
the UK has become much more right wing than

00:05:46.499 --> 00:05:49.279
many of us on the left would like to see.

00:05:49.279 --> 00:05:54.120
We'll have to see where the dominoes sort
of fall as far as that goes.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:06:02.839
But this is primarily a personal scandal with
within the context of the Conservative Party

00:06:02.839 --> 00:06:06.819
who will now choose a new leader and subsequently
there will be a new prime minister.

00:06:06.819 --> 00:06:10.979
Now, there could be follow on effects at the
time of the next election.

00:06:10.979 --> 00:06:15.910
And depending on what happens within the United
States in terms of the midterms in 2024, you

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:19.990
could certainly see a shifting dynamic in
the relationship between the UK and the U.S.

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:22.309
and in the UK's position and globally.

00:06:22.309 --> 00:06:24.139
None of that is happening right now.

00:06:24.139 --> 00:06:25.610
This is Johnson is out.

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:30.689
He will be replaced other than again this
sort of like cartoonish nature of Johnson,

00:06:30.689 --> 00:06:34.949
I don't anticipate, based on everything I'm
reading right now, that there will be any

00:06:34.949 --> 00:06:39.360
radical or substantive changes, certainly
to our relationship with the UK, but not a

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:40.360
good couple of.

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:46.620
Days for Boris Johnson and very much like
Trump, defiant until the final moment with

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:51.280
Trump, it was, well, making every claim about
how he was going to stay in power because

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:56.169
he really won and then just quietly leaving,
not even going to the inauguration with Boris

00:06:56.169 --> 00:07:03.099
Johnson for weeks and weeks remaining indignant
about, well, what do you mean, resign?

00:07:03.099 --> 00:07:04.099
Two days.

00:07:04.099 --> 00:07:08.029
Even when it was clear the pressure was overwhelming,
saying, why would I resign?

00:07:08.029 --> 00:07:33.309
And then I'm out and we'll see what the next

00:07:33.309 --> 00:08:26.159
step is.

